        "side": "new",
        "severity": "high",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Double free of mp_name when cpool was created before the error",
        "explanation": "pcfg.name is mp_name, and mlx5_hws_cnt_pool_init presumably copies pcfg into cpool->cfg. On the error path, mlx5_hws_cnt_pool_destroy(sh, cpool) already runs mlx5_free((void *)cpool->cfg.name) whenever cpool is non-NULL. This applies to failures after pool_init succeeds, such as dcs_alloc, raw_data_alloc, action_create and the guest-port action_create. The added mlx5_free(mp_name) then frees the same buffer a second time. It is only needed when cpool is NULL, because destroy returns early in that case.",
        "suggestion": "Free mp_name only when cpool == NULL, for example `if (cpool == NULL) mlx5_free(mp_name);`. Alternatively, make ownership explicit by clearing the pointer once the pool owns it.",
        "evidence": "\tmlx5_free(mp_name);",
        "confidence": 0.7,
        "id": "3704f87678e3",
